  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8cf72940f56fa4944b96a056293a7297, type: 3}
  m_Name: Tutorial
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  npcTalking: 
  _lines:
  - The director is looking to distinguish Figures from normal human patients.
  - Figures have "rendering anomolies", bodily atttributes that are mutations of
    normal flesh and bone.
  - (wonder what that looks like...)
  - The director wants me to use nails to mark these attributes...
  - Almost like an icepick lobotomy...I've only spectated one once, and that already
    made me feel sick.
  - I guess I'll have to be quick with the nails.
  - Accordingly, it makes sense that I need to interrogate them about potential attributes
    before marking.
  - Judging by the large pile they've provided, I assume they intend for me to mark
    as many attributes as I can.
  - The director also wants me to finalize my identification status of the patient
    at the end of the examination, once I'm sure I've marked all attributes.
  - This patient, Galatea, looks normal from the front, so I guess I'll check her
    back for any attributes.
  - I best be thorough.
  _nextNode: []
  examNext: 0
